* but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of
* MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.  See the
* GNU General Public License for more details.
*
* You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License
* along with this program; if not, write to the Free Software Foundation,
* Inc., 59 Temple Place - Suite 330, Boston, MA 02111-1307, USA.
*
* START-HISTORY:
* 18 Oct 26 dm  Written: encryption layer 3 (the XE conversion; gplsrc/sd_keyring.c).
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   CALL !KEYSET(name, key, id)
*
* name  the key name the XE;name conversion asks for (1 to 31 letters, digits, dots, dashes or underscores, folded to lower
*       case; a null name is "default", the key a bare XE uses)
* key   a 256 bit key as 44 base64 characters: what SDKEY() and SDRANDKEY() return
* id    returned: the key's id (8 hex digits) when it is in the ring; the null string and STATUS() 10213 (bad name), 10204 (the
*       key is not 44 characters), 10203 (it is not base64) or 10211 (the ring holds 16 keys) when it is not
*
* The ring is this process's own memory: cleared by LOGTO, by !KEYCLEAR and when the process ends, never written to a file, the
* audit trail or $COMO, and not handed to a phantom (a phantom that must decrypt calls !KEYSET itself).  A key set again under a
* name is kept beside the old one: the newest is the one new values are encrypted with, and values made under the older one can
* still be read.
*
* The key passes through the arguments of this call and so through the variables of the caller, which are the caller's to
* clear (key = '').
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
$catalog !keyset
$include keys.h

   key_id = ''
   key_id = sdext('set':@fm:key_name:@fm:key, @true, SD_KEYRING)

return
end
